[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So, as you may know, if you\'ve been on this channel before, I\'m a big fan of the original Ace Pro 2 Explorer Grip Combo. I\'ve taken it on many an adventure. This new version of the Explorer Cage or Grip, I may say that interchangeably throughout this video,'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is hugely improved in many areas, and it\'s very, very exciting to see how the Ace Pro 2 as a photography camera has evolved. I was there at the Insta 360 launch event in Frankfurt, and they have'

[00:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'sent me this camera for review. And this video is sponsored by them. So, please think of this as a showcase if you prefer rather than a critical review because I know it\'s sponsored. But rest assured, I have lots of negatives to'

[00:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'cover as well as positives because when I was at the event, Insta3 themselves said that they always read the comments of these videos and they listen to community feedback. So, I\'ve got some notes. So, what\'s new? The cage now'

[00:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'connects via USBC to the camera itself. And it works as one cohesive unit and feels very much like a traditional camera. You press the shutter, you can get a photo. You have a zoom rocker that'

[01:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you can either gradually zoom into or press one way or the other to zoom in and out quickly. And you also have a back dial for your settings. You can customize this back dial in a number of ways. There\'s two settings I really like'

[01:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'so far. I like shutter speed priority or I like to just be able to toggle between the JPEG filters. Speaking of the filters, in collaboration with Leica, there are now four new filters. My'

[01:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'favorite of which is called Leica Eternal, which you shall probably see a lot of throughout this video, and also the Leica monochrome, which you will also see a lot of throughout this video. And perhaps the biggest update is you'

[01:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'can now add different lenses to the front of your Ace Pro 2. You have an ultra wide lens and a close-up lens and also a cinematic lens, too. And cinematic just means it\'s an anamorphic'

[01:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'lens, which is quite exciting, actually. Now, the wide angle, right, when I first saw this, I didn\'t think it was the best idea. And then there\'s an ultra wide lens.'

[02:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I mean, just what everybody wants, a ridiculously wide lens. Aren\'t action cameras wide enough? But actually, it\'s the most fun to play with. Just the most fun. And I actually think I got some of'

[02:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'my favorite photographs of the entire year with this wide angle lens, which was from this mall. Love them. And it just gives you such an interesting perspective with that ultra wide. And my goodness, is it ultra wide.'

[02:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; Past Emily, who didn\'t want this lens, is such a party pooper. This is my new favorite lens. So cool seeing the world in this perspective. Wow. &gt;&gt; And then in terms of video, having the'

[02:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'ultra wide attachment will probably open up more creative ideas as well, cuz you\'ll be able to get the camera into stranger places and see more of the frame. So, I\'m excited to use the wide-angle lens more. And I am pretty sure you\'ll be seeing more of it on this'

[02:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'channel actually cuz it\'s so cool. It\'s been ages since I\'ve done wideangle photography and I just had a ball with it honestly. It is wide enough that you\'ll see the circular elements of the lens and even see your fingers in frame.'

[03:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'My fingers are in the frame here. So, you have to kind of hold it like this like a proper dod cam [laughter] so that you don\'t get your fingers in the way. So, the way that these lenses'

[03:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'work is it\'s completely done adapted, but you do have a setting in the menu where you can tell the camera which lens it has on. With the close-up lens, it\'s well worth turning the features on in the menu because it enables focus peaking and you can see what\'s in focus'

[03:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in the frame. This lens gives me two moments of joy. First of all, it solves a very big problem I had with the Ace Pro 2 originally, and that\'s the minimal focus distance is quite far away.'

[03:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Sometimes when I was using it as a selfie vlogging camera, the background would be perfectly in focus and my face would be slightly out of focus. With this lens attachment now, you can use it vlogging just fine. Has this new close-up attachment fixed the minimum'

[03:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'focus distance problem? I\'ve got it on people. And then you can do it presumably closer. I don\'t really want to get that close because this is without and I think on'

[04:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'my other camera if I\'ve been this close I\'ve been slightly soft and the background has been in focus. And then secondly, now we have a closeup POV camera. It\'s quite small. It\'s quite'

[04:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'easy to mount places with a magic arm. And now all of a sudden with this lens attachment, we have much more creative opportunities than we had before with this camera because it just wouldn\'t focus close enough in the past. And now'

[04:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it will. Then the cinematic lens is an anamorphic lens. And because the Ace Pro 2 will shoot in 4x3 open gate, you actually can get some very cool effects with it. So, my first negative or just feedback because I\'m sure you could fix'

[04:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this in firmware is I\'m really not a fan of faffing around in the menus every time I want to change lenses. I would love like in the main menu where you have video and pure shot and all the other options. If you could have a'

[05:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'close-up icon and then it\'ll know automatically. I think that would be a much more easy accessible way to do it than having it in the menus as it is currently. Oh, and just to mention quickly, if you have noticed that the front looks a little bit different on'

[05:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the Ace Pro 2 that I\'m showing in this video compared to previous versions, it\'s exactly the same camera. They\'ve just changed the design of the front a little bit. So, if you have an older Ace Pro 2 with the square front mount, it\'s fine. All of these things will still'

[05:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'work with it. So, going back to the updated Explorer Grip, you do have to charge it now as it communicates with the camera, and you can even use that to top up the camera when you\'re out and about, which is quite cool. I think the'

[05:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'battery life on the Ace Pro 2 to begin with is really good. But if you are shooting for longer days, having a backup battery within the grip itself is a really cool idea. Going even back to like using the 360 cameras with Insta 360. One thing I think that the company'

[05:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'have always done really well is seamlessly integrating the hardware and the software. So, I was a little bit concerned when I first started setting this up that it might be unreliable. It might slow me down. But honestly, you'

[06:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'turn the camera on and within seconds it\'s automatically synced and you can start shooting. It is absolutely foolproof, Emily proof, everything proof. It\'s super super user friendly to the point actually that I left it in the'

[06:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'cage for the whole trip to Frankfurt and just forgot that it was an action cam. I was just picking it up and I\'m like, "Yeah, it\'s just a tiny camera. It\'s it doesn\'t even feel like an action camera anymore because it just it\'s so'

[06:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'cohesive." What else is new? There\'s a cute little screen shield which is adorable and it comes on and off via magnets which is music to my ears because I live in quite a dull place in England and I don\'t often have problems'

[06:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'where it\'s blindingly bright on the screen. But I can totally see this being really handy if you do live in those brighter climates. So in my previous review of the Ace Pro 2 for photography, a lot of the negatives I had in that'

[06:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'video have been addressed and updated in this version, which is wonderful. But there\'s one negative that I would love to see be fixed and it\'s really the last one standing as far as I\'m concerned. And that is yes, we have a two times'

[07:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'crop in the photography on the Ace Pro 2, but even at its most zoomedin setting, it\'s still [music] pretty wide. I would love if we could have a lens attachment that makes it like 35 mil. 40 mil would be the dream, but that might'

[07:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'be pushing it a bit too far. If we could have just an attachment that gives you a more traditional street photography sort of lens, I would be over the moon. That would just be the icing on the cake. We\'re done. We\'re done. We can finished.'

[07:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Everything\'s done. There\'s nothing else to improve. Love it. As it stands, you do have quite wide angle options. You can get more normal looking photos out of the two times zoom in this camera.'

[07:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Obviously, because it is an action camera at the bones of it, it does lend towards wide angle photography. Oh, I forgot the other accessory as well. This one\'s really cool, actually. They\'ve brought out a pocket printer and you can buy this in an accessory bundle with the'

[08:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Ace Pro 2 and you can attach it onto the Ace Pro 2 and it\'s like a little Polaroid. This is also an accessory that works really seamlessly as well. Once it\'s connected via Bluetooth, which takes one button, there\'s a little'

[08:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'printer icon that shows up and then you can send things to the printer. Now, to set your expectations, this printer is incredibly high quality, and it looks like little Polaroids, but it\'s not very fast. It\'s not very fast. I recently did a tiny printer video where I went'

[08:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'through my favorite tiny printers. And in second place is my delightful Canon Selfie. And that prints in the same way that this Insta 360 one does, where it does each color one by one. And what'

[08:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'results in that is a really high quality print at the end. However, it does take a little bit of time. Not massive amounts, but like you you\'re looking at over a minute per print. The Insta 360 is sort of the best of both worlds'

[08:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'because you have the little dinky Polaroidesque images, but the really high quality prints like the Canon selfie. So, the printer is really cool. However, it\'s intended to be attached to the camera and I just would never use it'

[09:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'like that. I would stick it in my bag and use it as like a a separate accessory. It\'s great to keep in your bag and just lob out whenever you want to print a photo, but I wouldn\'t necessarily attach it to the camera personally. Your mileage may vary. So, I have on the whole been incredibly'

[09:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'impressed with this new accessory kit for a camera that I already loved and I\'m genuinely so so happy with so many of the photos that I got from this trip. But, I promised you some negatives and here are some juicy negatives. This one'

[09:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I\'ve noticed in the comments, so I\'m not the only person to have noticed this. In the 50 megapixel photo mode, there is a little delay after you take the photo as it writes to the card. And while it\'s'

[09:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'writing, you can\'t do blooming anything. So, you can\'t change the filter. You can\'t change the zoom. You can\'t change the photo mode. I don\'t even want to take a photograph. I understand that it needs to write to the card before it can'

[09:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'take a photograph again. But if we could do it where you could change your settings as it\'s writing, that would make the whole process so much better because there is a little bit of a delay. Now, you can circumvent this by just using the 12.5 megapixel mode and'

[10:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'then it writes to the card so much faster and then you\'re back up and running. To give you a real world example of this, I was shooting some really wide angle photography at a junction and I was waiting for people or bicycles to come over the junction so I'

[10:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'had an interesting subject. In the 50 megapixel mode, I had one shot because once I\'d taken one shot, there was like a two or three second delay before I could take another photo and by then the bike had gone. In the 12.5 megapixel mode, it was much more easily'

[10:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'manageable. And you could have utilized the slow burst mode in retrospect, but I didn\'t think to do it at the time. But yeah, if there was any tweaks that Insta 360 could make to just make writing to the camera a little bit faster or even just be allowed to change the settings'

[10:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and stuff as you wait, it would be so so good. Otherwise, I find myself using the 12.5 megapixel mode more often than not, it gives you more than enough pixels to work with, and it\'s much snappier to use. So, as much as I love the upgrades of the Explorer Cage or the Explorer'

[11:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Grip, nine times out of 10, I will be using the updated one over the original metal one, but there are a couple of drawbacks that I can think of with the new grip. One being it\'s one extra thing to charge, and if it\'s not charged, it'

[11:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'won\'t bloom work. whereas the old one was just a slab of metal, so it didn\'t matter if it was charged or not. You couldn\'t charge it. And two, because it does have a mic input and dials and buttons, it\'s not weather sealed. The'

[11:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'camera is completely waterproof, but the grip itself is not weather sealed. So, if you\'re going out taking photography on a rainy day, you can\'t do that with this grip without risking breaking it. Conversely, on the original grip, it\'s'

[11:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'just a metal cage. I took it through a blooming waterfall in Iceland. like it doesn\'t matter. It\'s completely weather sealed cuz it\'s not got any electrical elements in it. This is like a little bit less robust than the action camera'

[11:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'itself. Like I\'ve dropped my action camera with the cage on it and it would break the floor before it would break the action camera. Whereas this cage or grip that you\'ve got the action camera in is less robust than the action camera'

[12:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'itself. And it\'s just something to bear in mind. If you\'re travel and doing street photography and lifestyle photography doesn\'t matter in the slightest. If you\'re doing more adventure style stuff, then you do have to be aware that if the weather changes, you might have to take it out of the'

[12:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'grip. So, the overall experience using this is so much like any other of the plethora of tiny cameras that I\'ve taken out with me over the years. I had it on my lovely little uh PGY Tech camera strap. It was so seamless to use, so'

[12:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'much fun to use, and it\'s a proper tactile nice experience. It doesn\'t feel like an action camera at all. But then you have, of course, all the added benefits of it actually being an action camera where we have super slow motion,'

[12:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'where we have open gate video, we have really cool time-lapses, and it\'s all automated for you. So, you don\'t have to be too techy in order to do them. You have fantastic stabilization, you have pure shot video. On the video side, it\'s'

[13:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'just superb. And the audio out of it is brilliant as well. Look at all the buildings. I am loving the upgrades to the Explorer Grip so far. It really turns it into a'

[13:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'very tactile experience. It doesn\'t feel any different than a normal camera. Now, the shutter button works instantly. Everything connects really quickly. It\'s just a very interesting camera system.'

[13:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'You can add in like an extra Bluetooth mic or use the input jack on the grip to add in some professional audio, but the built-in microphone is bloody brilliant. It really does become like this'

[13:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'all-in-one little camera. You can even use the screen as like a tilt back as like a mini tripod, which I used several times when I was shooting time-lapses. And now we have different lenses, and it\'s just like an ecosystem in and of'

[13:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'itself that offers so much value. So, I\'m a big fan of where this line of cameras is heading. I\'m just really, really happy to see all of the updates. What do you think of all the new updated accessories? Are you going to be adding'

